{"name":"Adobe Straw","hex":"#c3a998","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"adobe","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An unburnt brick dried in the sun.","The earth from which such bricks are made."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/adobe"},{"term":"straw","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dried stalk of a cereal plant.","Such dried stalks considered collectively; this bulk matter may be a chief salable product, a by-product, fodder, bedding, or green manure, depending on region and on current market conditions."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of straw.","Of a pale, yellowish beige colour, like that of a dried straw."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/straw"}],"entries":[{"title":"Adobe","blocks":[{"text":"Adobe is a building material made from loam and organic materials. Adobe is Spanish for mudbrick. In some English-speaking regions of Spanish heritage, such as the Southwestern United States, the term is used to refer to any kind of earthen construction, or various architectural styles like Pueblo Revival or Territorial Revival. Most adobe buildings are similar in appearance to cob and rammed earth buildings. Adobe is among the earliest building materials, and is used throughout the world."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Adobe_wall_%28detail%29_1.jpg/330px-Adobe_wall_%28detail%29_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adobe"},{"title":"Straw","blocks":[{"text":"Straw is an agricultural byproduct consisting of the dry stalks of cereal plants after the grain and chaff have been removed. It makes up about half of the yield by weight of cereal crops such as barley, oats, rice, rye and wheat. It has a number of different uses, including fuel, livestock bedding and fodder, thatching and basket making."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Rice_straw.jpg/330px-Rice_straw.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Straw"},{"title":"Straw (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Straw is a colour, a tone of pale yellow, the colour of straw. The Latin word stramineus, with the same meaning, is often used in describing nature."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Strohr%C3%A4der.jpg/330px-Strohr%C3%A4der.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Straw_(colour)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/AdobeSurfaceCoatingRenewalOnWall.jpg/500px-AdobeSurfaceCoatingRenewalOnWall.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/AdobeSurfaceCoatingRenewalOnWall.jpg/500px-AdobeSurfaceCoatingRenewalOnWall.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Renewal of the surface coating of an adobe wall in Chamisal, New Mexico","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAdobeSurfaceCoatingRenewalOnWall.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Qasroddasht.JPG/500px-Qasroddasht.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Qasroddasht.JPG/1280px-Qasroddasht.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Qasroddasht.JPG/500px-Qasroddasht.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Adobe walls separate urban gardens in Shiraz, Iran","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AQasroddasht.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/San_Pedro_de_Atacama_church.jpg/500px-San_Pedro_de_Atacama_church.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&u